    content: "The topography of Embu and Mbeere is characterized by highlands, midlands, lowlands, hills and valleys typical of Kenya’s eastern highlands. Due to the presence of Mt. Kenya, the landscape is quite dissected with landforms that cascade in a south-easterly direction. Altitudes range from 5,199 m above sea level at the top of Mt. Kenya in Embu to 570 m at the confluence of the Tana and Mutonga rivers in Mbeere. The upper parts of Embu in parts of Kyeni, Manyatta and Runyenjes have altitudes ranging 1500 to 4500 metres. The middle parts covering Nembure and Kithimu fall between 1200 to 1500 metres. The lower parts covering much of Mbeere comprise gently sloping to rolling terrain while the Mwea-Makima area is relatively flat. The major hills in the County include Karue, Kirimiri and Maranga in Embu, while in Mbeere; there are Kiang’ombe, Kiambere, Kianjiru, Kirigo and other minor hills.",
