    category: "heritage_sites_and_places",
    title: "Kubukubu",
    content: "Kubukubu was a Mau Mau leader who lived with his group in Kirimiri forest, near Runyenjes. He was caught during the struggle for independence and burnt. The then colonial rulers forced the local people to clap as Kubukubu was being burnt. This angered many people and after the incident, other young men joined the Mau Mau fighters in the forest. The Kubukubu Memorial Primary School is built at the site where the great fighter was burnt, and so named in his honour.",
